A||||10||wxxo||gt vs se...whats the difference||||1||
Z||000000||wxxo||07-10-2000||12:15 PM||||what exactly separates say an 86se v6 4spd from an 86 gt (aside from the body)? is the gt still faster? just curious.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||07-10-2000||12:20 PM||||The engine and transmission are exactly the same.  The GT may have different springs and shocks (not sure on the 86).  The SE is a bit lighter and should technically be a bit faster than the GT.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-10-2000||02:37 PM||||An '86SE is identical to an '85 GT with the exception of the 3rd brake light and some trim.  The '86 GT is a fastback whereas the '86SE is a notchback.  Might weigh a couple of pounds less, but not enough to make any difference.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000003||wxxo||07-10-2000||03:08 PM||||I see. that doesnt make much sense.i like the fastback look however i have a notchback. grass is always greener huh. how about the formula?? i know about the suspension in the 88s but what else???||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||07-10-2000||09:30 PM||||I think the formula is just a later model SE.I too have an 86SE that will soon be a fastback.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-10-2000||10:37 PM||||If you want a Formula, just take an '88 GT and remove the fastback, the aero fascias and most of the options (except for the V6, the wing, and the wheels).  There you go.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||07-10-2000||11:53 PM||||I just heard someone say that there was no such thing as an S/E made with a V6 5spd,that they only came with a 4spd!<BR>Ever seen one before with a 5spd?<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||07-11-2000||05:07 AM||||The 87 SE V6's come with 5 speeds.  I don't think there were very many 87 SE V6's made, tho..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||shain||07-11-2000||05:14 AM||||in 1985, (the last year for the S/E)  you could only get a v6 w/ a 4 spd tranny. <BR> (86 they changed the name to SE but still had only a 4 spd). <BR>1987 was the first year for the v6 w/5spd* <P><BR>*actually, in 86 the fiero GT was the first recipient of the new 5 spd(getrag) tranny.  but only 2550 fiero GT's got that transaxle!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||shain||07-11-2000||05:25 AM||||wow mike! you have a rare car!! its one of 2550 out of the 17660 gts made that year!<BR>also there were only 3875 87 SE's made that year, (also the last year for SE) and only half of those had the 5 spd!! good fieros to get your hands on !!<P>wow am i a fountain of knowledge or what??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
